  "id": "08-fifo-oldest-layer-first",
  "description": "FIFO CONSUMES THE OLDEST COSTED LAYER, AND THE ANSWER IS NEITHER THE AVERAGE NOR LIFO'S. Three receipts build three layers: PUR-1 10.0000 @ 100.0000 = 1000.0000, PUR-2 10.0000 @ 120.0000 = 1200.0000, PUR-3 5.0000 @ 80.0000 = 400.0000. SAL-1 issues 15.0000 on 05-Apr, when only the first two layers exist: it takes ALL of PUR-1 (1000.0000) and 5.0000 of PUR-2 at 120.0000 (600.0000) -> consumed 1600.0000, leaving PUR-2 holding 5.0000 units at 600.0000. SAL-2 issues 8.0000 on 07-Apr: the rest of PUR-2 (600.0000) plus 3.0000 of PUR-3 at 80.0000 (240.0000) -> consumed 840.0000. Closing 2.0000 units, all of them PUR-3's, at 160.0000, rate 80.0000. Total consumed 2440.0000. Conservation: 0 + 2600.0000 - 2440.0000 = 160.0000. THE THREE METHODS DISAGREE ON THE SAME MOVEMENTS AND THAT IS THE POINT: this item closes at 160.0000 under FIFO, 200.0000 under LIFO (fixture 09) and 190.0000 under weighted average - which is why a report that prints a stock value has to print the basis beside it, and why switching an item's method MOVES THE BALANCE SHEET.",
